{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.18","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/masum1834e/pytorch?scriptVersionId=370286280\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Neural Network Modules\nIn PyTorch, things like `nn.Linear` and `nn.Embedding` are called **Neural Network Modules (or Layers)**.\n\nThere are several categories of these modules. Below is a comprehensive practical reference of the built-in `torch.nn` modules.\n\n## Fully Connected Layers\n\nUsed in MLPs, classifiers, and neural networks.\n\n| PyTorch Module  | Purpose                             |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `nn.Linear`     | Fully connected layer               |\n| `nn.LazyLinear` | Linear layer that infers input size |\n| `nn.Bilinear`   | Bilinear transformation             |\n| `nn.Identity`   | Passes input unchanged              |\n\n## Embedding Layers\n\nUsed mainly in NLP, language models, and categorical data.\n\n| PyTorch Module    | Purpose                                 |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `nn.Embedding`    | Maps integer indices to vectors         |\n| `nn.EmbeddingBag` | Aggregates embeddings using sum or mean |\n\n## Convolution Layers\n\nUsed in CNNs, computer vision, and spatial data.\n\n| PyTorch Module           | Purpose                        |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| `nn.Conv1d`              | 1D convolution                 |\n| `nn.Conv2d`              | 2D convolution                 |\n| `nn.Conv3d`              | 3D convolution                 |\n| `nn.ConvTranspose1d`     | 1D transposed convolution      |\n| `nn.ConvTranspose2d`     | 2D transposed convolution      |\n| `nn.ConvTranspose3d`     | 3D transposed convolution      |\n| `nn.LazyConv1d`          | Lazy 1D convolution            |\n| `nn.LazyConv2d`          | Lazy 2D convolution            |\n| `nn.LazyConv3d`          | Lazy 3D convolution            |\n| `nn.LazyConvTranspose1d` | Lazy transposed 1D convolution |\n| `nn.LazyConvTranspose2d` | Lazy transposed 2D convolution |\n| `nn.LazyConvTranspose3d` | Lazy transposed 3D convolution |\n\n## Pooling Layers\n\nUsed for reducing spatial or temporal dimensions.\n\n| PyTorch Module           | Purpose                     |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------- |\n| `nn.MaxPool1d`           | 1D max pooling              |\n| `nn.MaxPool2d`           | 2D max pooling              |\n| `nn.MaxPool3d`           | 3D max pooling              |\n| `nn.AvgPool1d`           | 1D average pooling          |\n| `nn.AvgPool2d`           | 2D average pooling          |\n| `nn.AvgPool3d`           | 3D average pooling          |\n| `nn.AdaptiveMaxPool1d`   | Adaptive 1D max pooling     |\n| `nn.AdaptiveMaxPool2d`   | Adaptive 2D max pooling     |\n| `nn.AdaptiveMaxPool3d`   | Adaptive 3D max pooling     |\n| `nn.AdaptiveAvgPool1d`   | Adaptive 1D average pooling |\n| `nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d`   | Adaptive 2D average pooling |\n| `nn.AdaptiveAvgPool3d`   | Adaptive 3D average pooling |\n| `nn.FractionalMaxPool2d` | Fractional max pooling      |\n| `nn.FractionalMaxPool3d` | Fractional max pooling      |\n| `nn.LPPool1d`            | L-pooling 1D                |\n| `nn.LPPool2d`            | L-pooling 2D                |\n| `nn.LPPool3d`            | L-pooling 3D                |\n| `nn.MaxUnpool1d`         | Reverse max pooling 1D      |\n| `nn.MaxUnpool2d`         | Reverse max pooling 2D      |\n| `nn.MaxUnpool3d`         | Reverse max pooling 3D      |\n\n## Activation Functions\n\nThese introduce non-linearity into neural networks.\n\n**Most commonly used**\n\n| Module          | Purpose                                  |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `nn.ReLU`       | ReLU activation                          |\n| `nn.GELU`       | GELU activation; popular in Transformers |\n| `nn.SiLU`       | SiLU / Swish                             |\n| `nn.Sigmoid`    | Maps values to 0–1                       |\n| `nn.Tanh`       | Maps values to −1 to 1                   |\n| `nn.LeakyReLU`  | Leaky ReLU                               |\n| `nn.Softmax`    | Converts logits to probabilities         |\n| `nn.LogSoftmax` | Log of softmax                           |\n\n**Complete activation module list**\n\n```\nnn.ELU\nnn.CELU\nnn.GELU\nnn.GLU\nnn.Hardshrink\nnn.Hardsigmoid\nnn.Hardswish\nnn.Hardtanh\nnn.LeakyReLU\nnn.LogSigmoid\nnn.LogSoftmax\nnn.Mish\nnn.MultiheadAttentio\nnnn.PReLU\nnn.ReLU\nnn.ReLU6\nnn.RReLU\nnn.SELU\nnn.Sigmoid\nnn.SiLU\nnn.Softmax\nnn.Softmax2d\nnn.Softmi\nnnn.Softplus\nnn.Softshrink\nnn.Softsig\nnnn.Tanh\nnn.Tanhshrink\nnn.Threshold\n```\n\nNote: `nn.MultiheadAttention` is technically an attention module, not a conventional activation function.\n\n## Normalization Layers\n\nUsed to stabilize and improve training.\n\n| Module                  | Purpose                             |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `nn.BatchNorm1d`        | Batch normalization for 1D features |\n| `nn.BatchNorm2d`        | Batch normalization for images      |\n| `nn.BatchNorm3d`        | Batch normalization for 3D data     |\n| `nn.LazyBatchNorm1d`    | Lazy 1D batch norm                  |\n| `nn.LazyBatchNorm2d`    | Lazy 2D batch norm                  |\n| `nn.LazyBatchNorm3d`    | Lazy 3D batch norm                  |\n| `nn.SyncBatchNorm`      | Synchronized batch normalization    |\n| `nn.LayerNorm`          | Layer normalization                 |\n| `nn.GroupNorm`          | Group normalization                 |\n| `nn.InstanceNorm1d`     | Instance normalization              |\n| `nn.InstanceNorm2d`     | Instance normalization for images   |\n| `nn.InstanceNorm3d`     | Instance normalization for 3D data  |\n| `nn.LazyInstanceNorm1d` | Lazy instance norm                  |\n| `nn.LazyInstanceNorm2d` | Lazy instance norm                  |\n| `nn.LazyInstanceNorm3d` | Lazy instance norm                  |\n| `nn.LocalResponseNorm`  | Local response normalization        |\n| `nn.RMSNorm`            | Root Mean Square normalization      |\n\n## Dropout Layers\n\nUsed to reduce overfitting.\n\n| Module                   | Purpose                            |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `nn.Dropout`             | Randomly drops individual elements |\n| `nn.Dropout1d`           | Drops channels/features            |\n| `nn.Dropout2d`           | Drops entire image channels        |\n| `nn.Dropout3d`           | Drops entire 3D channels           |\n| `nn.AlphaDropout`        | Dropout compatible with SELU       |\n| `nn.FeatureAlphaDropout` | Feature-wise AlphaDropout          |\n\n## Recurrent Layers (RNN)\n\nUsed for sequential data.\n\n| Module        | Purpose                        |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `nn.RNN`      | Basic recurrent neural network |\n| `nn.LSTM`     | Long Short-Term Memory         |\n| `nn.GRU`      | Gated Recurrent Unit           |\n| `nn.RNNCell`  | Single RNN cell                |\n| `nn.LSTMCell` | Single LSTM cell               |\n| `nn.GRUCell`  | Single GRU cell                |\n\n## Transformer / Attention Layers\n\nUsed in GPT, BERT, LLMs, and other Transformer architectures.\n\n| Module                       | Purpose                   |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `nn.Transformer`             | Complete Transformer      |\n| `nn.TransformerEncoder`      | Transformer encoder stack |\n| `nn.TransformerDecoder`      | Transformer decoder stack |\n| `nn.TransformerEncoderLayer` | Single encoder layer      |\n| `nn.TransformerDecoderLayer` | Single decoder layer      |\n| `nn.MultiheadAttention`      | Multi-head attention      |\n\n## Padding Layers\n\n| Module                | Purpose                |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `nn.ZeroPad1d`        | 1D zero padding        |\n| `nn.ZeroPad2d`        | 2D zero padding        |\n| `nn.ZeroPad3d`        | 3D zero padding        |\n| `nn.ConstantPad1d`    | 1D constant padding    |\n| `nn.ConstantPad2d`    | 2D constant padding    |\n| `nn.ConstantPad3d`    | 3D constant padding    |\n| `nn.ReflectionPad1d`  | 1D reflection padding  |\n| `nn.ReflectionPad2d`  | 2D reflection padding  |\n| `nn.ReflectionPad3d`  | 3D reflection padding  |\n| `nn.ReplicationPad1d` | 1D replication padding |\n| `nn.ReplicationPad2d` | 2D replication padding |\n| `nn.ReplicationPad3d` | 3D replication padding |\n| `nn.CircularPad1d`    | 1D circular padding    |\n| `nn.CircularPad2d`    | 2D circular padding    |\n| `nn.CircularPad3d`    | 3D circular padding    |\n\n## Loss Functions\n\nUsed to calculate how wrong the model's predictions are.\n\n| Module                             | Purpose                           |\n| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `nn.L1Loss`                        | Mean Absolute Error               |\n| `nn.MSELoss`                       | Mean Squared Error                |\n| `nn.CrossEntropyLoss`              | Classification loss               |\n| `nn.BCELoss`                       | Binary Cross Entropy              |\n| `nn.BCEWithLogitsLoss`             | BCE combined with sigmoid         |\n| `nn.NLLLoss`                       | Negative Log Likelihood           |\n| `nn.NLLLoss2d`                     | 2D negative log likelihood        |\n| `nn.CTCLoss`                       | Sequence alignment loss           |\n| `nn.PoissonNLLLoss`                | Poisson negative log likelihood   |\n| `nn.GaussianNLLLoss`               | Gaussian negative log likelihood  |\n| `nn.KLDivLoss`                     | KL divergence                     |\n| `nn.HuberLoss`                     | Huber loss                        |\n| `nn.SmoothL1Loss`                  | Smooth L1 loss                    |\n| `nn.HingeEmbeddingLoss`            | Hinge embedding loss              |\n| `nn.MarginRankingLoss`             | Ranking loss                      |\n| `nn.MultiLabelMarginLoss`          | Multi-label margin loss           |\n| `nn.MultiLabelSoftMarginLoss`      | Multi-label soft margin loss      |\n| `nn.MultiMarginLoss`               | Multi-class margin loss           |\n| `nn.SoftMarginLoss`                | Soft margin loss                  |\n| `nn.CosineEmbeddingLoss`           | Cosine embedding loss             |\n| `nn.TripletMarginLoss`             | Triplet loss                      |\n| `nn.TripletMarginWithDistanceLoss` | Triplet loss with custom distance |\n| `nn.LinearCrossEntropyLoss`        | Linear cross-entropy loss         |\n| `nn.AdaptiveLogSoftmaxWithLoss`    | Efficient large-class loss        |\n\n## Distance Functions\n\n| Module                | Purpose           |\n| --------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `nn.CosineSimilarity` | Cosine similarity |\n| `nn.PairwiseDistance` | Pairwise distance |\n\n## M. Vision / Image Processing Modules\n\n| Module                    | Purpose                                 |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `nn.Upsample`             | Upsampling                              |\n| `nn.UpsamplingNearest2d`  | Nearest-neighbor upsampling             |\n| `nn.UpsamplingBilinear2d` | Bilinear upsampling                     |\n| `nn.PixelShuffle`         | Rearranges channels into spatial pixels |\n| `nn.PixelUnshuffle`       | Reverse pixel shuffle                   |\n| `nn.ChannelShuffle`       | Rearranges channels                     |\n| `nn.Flatten`              | Flattens dimensions                     |\n| `nn.Unflatten`            | Restores dimensions                     |\n| `nn.Unfold`               | Extracts sliding local blocks           |\n| `nn.Fold`                 | Combines blocks into output             |\n\n## N. Container Modules\n\nThese are used to combine multiple layers.\n\n| Module             | Purpose                                   |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `nn.Sequential`    | Sequentially executes layers              |\n| `nn.ModuleList`    | List of registered modules                |\n| `nn.ModuleDict`    | Dictionary of registered modules          |\n| `nn.ParameterList` | List of trainable parameters              |\n| `nn.ParameterDict` | Dictionary of trainable parameters        |\n| `nn.Module`        | Base class for all neural network modules |\n| `nn.Container`     | Base container class                      |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Linear\n\n`torch.nn.Linear` is one of the fundamental building blocks of neural networks. It performs a **linear transformation** on input data using weights and biases.\n\nA Linear layer calculates:\n\n$$ Y = XW^T + b $$\n\nWhere:\n\n- $X$ = Input data\n- $W$ = Weight matrix (learnable parameters)\n- $W^T$ = Transpose of the weight matrix\n- $b$ = Bias vector (learnable parameters)\n- $Y$ = Output\n\nIn simple terms:\n\n1. Take the input.\n2. Multiply it by weights.\n3. Add bias.\n4. Return the result.","metadata":{"_uuid":"8f2839f25d086af736a60e9eeb907d3b93b6e0e5","_cell_guid":"b1076dfc-b9ad-4769-8c92-a6c4dae69d19"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\n\nlayer = nn.Linear(\n    in_features=3,\n    out_features=2\n)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-16T13:08:35.18498Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-16T13:08:35.18526Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.934412Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-16T13:08:35.185234Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.933475Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"code","source":"layer","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.936608Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.937185Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.945178Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.937145Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.944048Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":2,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"Linear(in_features=3, out_features=2, bias=True)"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":2},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"What do these arguments mean?\n\n- `in_features=3`: Every input sample must have 3 features.\n- `out_features=2`: The layer produces 2 output features.\n- `bias=True`: The layer includes a learnable bias.\n\n## Weights and Biases","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"layer.weight.shape","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.946617Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.946961Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.973649Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.946927Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.972831Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":3,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"torch.Size([2, 3])"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"code","source":"layer.weight","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.974849Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.975655Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-16T13:08:39.11682Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-16T13:08:38.975628