res |\n| `bias` | Whether to include a learnable bias (`True` by default) |\n| `device` | Device where parameters are allocated (e.g. CPU or CUDA) |\n| `dtype` | Data type of parameters (e.g. `torch.float32`, `torch.float16`) |\n\n\n## Learn Weights (Linear)\n\nThis is where neural networks become interesting. Initially, PyTorch initializes weights and biases with values that are not necessarily useful for your task.\n\nDuring training, the model learns better values using:\n\n1. Forward propagation.\n2. Loss calculation.\n3. Backpropagation.\n4. Optimizer updates.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\n\n# 1. Create Linear layer\nlayer = nn.Linear(2, 1)\n\n# Set known initial weights and bias\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    layer.weight.copy_(torch.tensor([[0.5, 0.3]]))\n    layer.bias.copy_(torch.tensor([0.1]))\n\n# Input and target\nx = torch.tensor([[2.0, 3.0]])\ntarget = torch.tensor([[5.0]])\n\n# Loss and optimizer\ncriterion = nn.MSELoss()\noptimizer = torch.optim.SGD(layer.parameters(), lr=0.01)\n\n# Print initial parameters\nprint(\"INITIAL PARAMETERS\")\nprint(\"Weight:\", layer.weight.data)\nprint(\"Bias:\", layer.bias.data)\n\n# Training loop\nfor epoch in range(5):\n\n    # Forward propagation\n    prediction = layer(x)\n\n    # Calculate loss\n    loss = criterion(prediction, target)\n\n    # Clear old gradients\n    optimizer.zero_grad()\n\n    # Backpropagation\n    loss.backward()\n\n    # Show gradients\n    print(f\"\\n--- Epoch {epoch + 1} ---\")\n    print(\"Prediction:\", prediction.item())\n    print(\"Loss:\", loss.item())\n    print(\"Weight gradients:\", layer.weight.grad)\n    print(\"Bias gradients:\", layer.bias.grad)\n\n    # Save old weights for comparison\n    old_weight = layer.weight.data.clone()\n    old_bias = layer.bias.data.clone()\n\n    # Update parameters\n    optimizer.step()\n\n    # Print updated parameters\n    print(\"Old weight:\", old_weight)\n    print(\"New weight:\", layer.weight.data)\n\n    print(\"Old bias:\", old_bias)\n    print(\"New bias:\", layer.bias.data)\n\nprint(\"\\nFINAL PARAMETERS\")\nprint(\"Weight:\", layer.weight.data)\nprint(\"Bias:\", layer.bias.data)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-16T13:08:39.311253Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-16T13:08:39.311528Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-16T13:08:45.403777Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-16T13:08:39.311504Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-16T13:08:45.40283Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"INITIAL PARAMETERS\nWeight: tensor([[0.5000, 0.3000]])\nBias: tensor([0.1000])\n\n--- Epoch 1 ---\nPrediction: 2.0\nLoss: 9.0\nWeight gradients: tensor([[-12., -18.]])\nBias gradients: tensor([-6.])\nOld weight: tensor([[0.5000, 0.3000]])\nNew weight: tensor([[0.6200, 0.4800]])\nOld bias: tensor([0.1000])\nNew bias: tensor([0.1600])\n\n--- Epoch 2 ---\nPrediction: 2.8400001525878906\nLoss: 4.665599346160889\nWeight gradients: tensor([[ -8.6400, -12.9600]])\nBias gradients: tensor([-4.3200])\nOld weight: tensor([[0.6200, 0.4800]])\nNew weight: tensor([[0.7064, 0.6096]])\nOld bias: tensor([0.1600])\nNew bias: tensor([0.2032])\n\n--- Epoch 3 ---\nPrediction: 3.4448001384735107\nLoss: 2.4186465740203857\nWeight gradients: tensor([[-6.2208, -9.3312]])\nBias gradients: tensor([-3.1104])\nOld weight: tensor([[0.7064, 0.6096]])\nNew weight: tensor([[0.7686, 0.7029]])\nOld bias: tensor([0.2032])\nNew bias: tensor([0.2343])\n\n--- Epoch 4 ---\nPrediction: 3.880255937576294\nLoss: 1.2538267374038696\nWeight gradients: tensor([[-4.4790, -6.7185]])\nBias gradients: tensor([-2.2395])\nOld weight: tensor([[0.7686, 0.7029]])\nNew weight: tensor([[0.8134, 0.7701]])\nOld bias: tensor([0.2343])\nNew bias: tensor([0.2567])\n\n--- Epoch 5 ---\nPrediction: 4.193784236907959\nLoss: 0.6499838829040527\nWeight gradients: tensor([[-3.2249, -4.8373]])\nBias gradients: tensor([-1.6124])\nOld weight: tensor([[0.8134, 0.7701]])\nNew weight: tensor([[0.8456, 0.818